From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mm/nommu: copy a private mapping that cannot share its region

A read-only private mapping of a file shares an existing region of that
file when it is a subset of it, or goes on the file's pages when the
filesystem maps directly.  Two cases failed instead:

- a subset of a region the process has mapped itself, such as its own
  executable's text: the new mapping lies partly inside that one, which
  a Maple Tree slot cannot hold, so it failed with -ENOMEM;
- a mapping that overlaps a region without being a subset, on a file
  that cannot be mapped directly: "Attempt to share mismatched mappings"
  and -EINVAL, which protects shared mappings' consistency.

libbacktrace maps parts of the running executable, some reaching past
its text into the symbol and line tables, so std::stacktrace had no
names or lines.  A private mapping in either case now gets a private
copy, as MAP_PRIVATE allows; shared mappings are unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
---
--- a/mm/nommu.c
+++ b/mm/nommu.c
@@ -1025,6 +1025,18 @@
 	       len, current->pid, current->comm);
 	show_mem();
 	return -ENOMEM;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Whether [start, end) would partly overlap one of mm's mappings.  A Maple
+ * Tree slot holds one VMA, so such a range cannot be registered.
+ */
+static bool nommu_overlaps_partly(struct mm_struct *mm, unsigned long start,
+				  unsigned long end)
+{
+	struct vm_area_struct *vma = find_vma_intersection(mm, start, end);
+
+	return vma && (vma->vm_start != start || vma->vm_end != end);
 }
 
 /*
@@ -1142,11 +1154,22 @@
 			 * mappings */
 			if ((pregion->vm_pgoff != pgoff || rpglen != pglen) &&
 			    !(pgoff >= pregion->vm_pgoff && pgend <= rpgend)) {
-				/* new mapping is not a subset of the region */
-				if (!(capabilities & NOMMU_MAP_DIRECT))
+				/* new mapping is not a subset of the region; a
+				 * private one gets a copy of its own */
+				if (!(capabilities & NOMMU_MAP_DIRECT) &&
+				    (vm_flags & VM_SHARED))
 					goto sharing_violation;
 				continue;
 			}
+
+			/* A private mapping inside one of this process's own
+			 * mappings of the region, such as a program reading
+			 * its own executable, gets a copy instead. */
+			start = pregion->vm_start;
+			start += (pgoff - pregion->vm_pgoff) << PAGE_SHIFT;
+			if (!(vm_flags & VM_SHARED) &&
+			    nommu_overlaps_partly(current->mm, start, start + len))
+				continue;
 
 			/* we've found a region we can share */
 			pregion->vm_usage++;
@@ -1200,6 +1223,12 @@
 				/* The VMA end must not wrap past TASK_SIZE. */
 				ret = -ENOMEM;
 				goto error_just_free;
+			} else if (!(vm_flags & VM_SHARED) &&
+				   (capabilities & NOMMU_MAP_COPY) &&
+				   nommu_overlaps_partly(current->mm, addr,
+							 addr + len)) {
+				/* As above: a copy, not the file's pages. */
+				capabilities &= ~NOMMU_MAP_DIRECT;
 			} else {
 				vma->vm_start = region->vm_start = addr;
 				vma->vm_end = region->vm_end = addr + len;
